  "details": "I've been getting some feedback that Modular Avatar breaks with 3.3.0. Looking at the reports, it seems post-build avatar validation has been strengthened, and this is aborting builds due to too-large menu icons, missing parameter entries, etc. This is all well and good, but it's clear that end-users will not look at the console, and the VRCSDK does not expose these errors anywhere else.\n\nI looked into exposing these errors from MA's own error reporting UI. However, I couldn't because:\n\n1. CheckAvatarForValidationIssues is private and async\n\n2. Build hooks cannot run async tasks\n\n3. RegisterBuildContentProcessedCallback and RegisterBuildErrorCallback are also private.\n\nPlease either provide an API to obtain these errors that can be called from a build hook context, or make them more prominent to avoid end-user confusion.",
